8. COMMON INTERVIEW QUESTION

Q: Why use Files.readString() instead of FileInputStream?

Answer:

FileInputStream reads the file as bytes and is useful when the JSON file should be sent as-is.

Files.readString() reads the entire file into a String, allowing us to modify placeholders such as ${name} and ${email} before sending the request.


